title: A pacer's sleep does not count the time the machine is away, so its log falls silent through a suspend.
pid: 1f18c53a-412a-4fd9-a0e8-77a42ef77abd
body: |2-
  On 2026-11-15 the log has nothing from 05:13:33 to 08:03:11, though the
  pacer polls every ten minutes. 'sleep' counts on a clock that stops
  while the machine is suspended, so the ten minutes begun at 05:13:33
  ran out only at 08:03:11: the machine was away for all but ten
  minutes of that time. No
  'curl' of the usage check was running at 08:02:50, so it was not a
  request hanging. Before the silence, 'usage could not be read' every
  ten minutes meant no network.
